Cell["\<\
Call getMSGElemFromMSGCorep[MSG], then use exactly that ordered operation \
list in init. getTBBandCorep is supported only for this MSGCorep-generated \
route.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"fd9f5814-e2d4-4b2d-b13a-7ec25654159c"],

Cell["\<\
The basis selected by init fixes single- or double-valued treatment: a scalar \
basis such as s is single valued, while the explicit {sup,sdn} spinor basis \
is double valued.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"822bd366-371a-4461-aed3-b8d7bedb650d"],

Cell["\<\
kset is a nonempty list of three-component reciprocal-fractional points. The \
function returns Null and prints one k-name line and one Grid per point; the \
Grid, rather than an Association, is the public presentation result.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"4953b46e-6556-4c6c-a3b6-175473bdfe1f"],

Cell["\<\
The optional MSGCorep and SpaceGroupIrep applications must be installed, and \
the user must execute Needs[\"MSGCorep`\"] before either MagneticTB wrapper \
is called. MagneticTB neither loads MSGCorep automatically nor replaces its \
calculation with an internal approximation.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"219a8603-07b7-4481-9f3e-eb4f96fae6da"],

Cell["\<\
getTBBandCorep returns $Failed and issues a message when the dependency is \
unavailable, the current init session is incompatible, H/rules/kset are \
malformed, or MSGCorep rejects the model. It does not repair the input or \
switch to an approximate fallback.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"f42ee5d6-2bcd-4141-92dd-2a13ff978c43"]
}, Closed]],

